<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch02-vector-products" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Vector Products from Quaternions to Area and Volume</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>Dot products measure angles and projections, cross products encode oriented area in space, and determinants measure signed area and volume. We develop their algebra from coordinates, then introduce constant linear and alternating measurements as a first special case of differential forms. The chapter closes with a quaternion rotation project and review.</p>
  </introduction>

